{
 "id": "drives",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "self_load_only": true,
 "depends_on": [],
 "area": "retina",
 "description": "THE DRIVE SYSTEM (block 207000) -- Dorner/Bach PSI/MicroPsi needs as first-class graph nodes. A Drive{name, target v_d, current c_d, critical v_0, weight, decay, gain, loss, half_life} with the MicroPsi demand equations as integer rules: urge = |v_d-c_d| (drive_urge); urgency = |v_d-c_d|*SCALE / max(1,|v_d-v_0|) (drive_urgency); the drive IS a decaying held quantity -- c_d <- Ashr(c_d, IDiv(now-last_tend, half_life)) reuses the 196000 staleness_decay scale2 atom (drive_decay); pleasure/displeasure = sign of delta c_d, the motivational reinforcers. A threat drive carries the 196000 freshness atom on its threat channel (drive_threat_precision/persist): a SHORT threat_half_life decays the precision below t_present (FEAR), a LONG one persists (ANXIETY) -- the fear<->anxiety minimal pair, the SAME PTSD knob. AFFILIATION is the social currency: a legitimacy_signal ingest (praise +gain, reproach -loss, scaled by the source's social_weight) is a rule (drive_affiliation_legitimacy); NURTURING is its complement and its ABSENCE is the 204000 w_supergraph~0 psychopathy knob (convergent glass-box). Each drive exposes an arousal_contrib for the modulator layer. Integer-native, NO Rust, NO new Term. OFF by default: every rule guards on the bound ModulatorState.enabled the measure adapter creates only on opt-in; absent it every existing path is byte-identical.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "drives",
  "description": "A minimal orthogonal set of needs (demands); goals are learned situations that satisfy/frustrate them. urge=|v_d-c_d|, urgency normalises by proximity to the critical extreme; the drive is a decaying held quantity (the 196000 scale2 atom); pleasure/displeasure = sign of delta c_d. Affiliation is the social currency, nurturing its complement (absence = psychopathy)."
 },
